apital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Director of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A to join Grafana Labs and help build and scale our Corporate FP&amp;amp;A function as the company enters its next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a pivotal leadership role responsible for building the financial infrastructure and operating cadence that power company-wide planning, forecasting, reporting, and decision-making. You will own key Corporate FP&amp;amp;A processes, including long-range planning, annual planning, consolidated P&amp;amp;L, Balance Sheet and Cash Flow forecasting, executive and Board reporting, while helping establish the rigor, systems, and insights required to support the company’s next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as a key partner to Finance, business leaders, and the executive leadership team, translating operating performance into clear financial insights and helping drive fast, informed decisions. The ideal candidate is a seasoned, results-oriented finance leader with strong business judgment, high integrity, and a track record of building scalable processes in complex, high-growth environments. You should be equally comfortable operating strategically and going deep into the details, with the ability to identify what needs to be built and raise the overall standard of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to build the foundation for Corporate FP&amp;amp;A at a high-growth global company. The role is fully remote and will report to the VP of Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the company-wide Corporate FP&amp;amp;A model and planning processes, including long-range planning, annual planning, monthly forecasting, and consolidated P&amp;amp;L, Balance Sheet, and Cash Flow forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive and Board reporting, delivering clear, decision-ready materials and commentary on business performance, key drivers, risks, opportunities, and operating leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously refine the company’s KPI and reporting architecture, including scorecards, dashboards, recurring business reviews, and analytical frameworks that leadership and investors can rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Accounting, Tax, and other Finance teams to support month-end close, flux reviews, and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and continuously improve Corporate FP&amp;amp;A operating rhythms, including close-to-insight timelines, clear ownership, metric definitions, and reporting processes designed to support the company’s next phase of growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the modernization of Finance processes, forecasting methodologies, and planning frameworks through systems, workflow automation, structured data, and AI to improve accuracy, scalability, and the quality of forward-looking insights as the business evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong cross-functional relationships with business and functional leaders, serving as a trusted partner on financial performance, resource allocation, and strategic decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, mentor, and develop a high-performing Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team, and support strategic initiatives such as M&amp;amp;A diligence and integration as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience across FP&amp;amp;A, Strategic Finance, Corporate Finance, or related disciplines, including meaningful experience at a leading technology company and ideally complementary experience in investment banking or buy-side investing. Experience in SaaS, enterprise software, or the broader technology sector is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate FP&amp;amp;A leadership experience, ideally in a public-company, newly public, or public-company-readiness environment, with exposure to quarterly close, executive reporting, Board reporting, and other rigorous financial operating cadences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful experience owning a consolidated P&amp;amp;L, company-wide forecast, and Balance Sheet and Cash Flow forecasting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced financial modeling and analytical skills, with the ability to build models from scratch, pressure-test assumptions, identify root causes, and translate complex analysis into clear, actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills, with experience preparing and presenting decision-ready materials to senior leadership and the Board, and influencing significant company decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to serve as a trusted business partner across functions and geographies, with strong business judgment and a track record of building effective cross-functional relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success as a change agent, improving forecasting, planning, reporting, and operating processes as organizations scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems and technical fluency, including experience with Pigment and AI tools, and a track record of automating financial processes and applying AI to Finance workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at multiple altitudes, from strategic thinking to detailed execution, while prioritizing competing demands and managing multiple projects in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A player-coach mindset with high attention to detail and the highest standards of integrity, credibility, and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;zfr3Q CDt4Ke &quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;C9DxTc &quot;&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;zfr3Q CDt4Ke &quot;&gt;In the United States, the OTE (On-Target Earnings) compensation range for this role is $260,000 - $312,000.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
